@arkology Confirmed in rendering meeting today, AtlasTexture just won't be supported as a source (at least for this PR) - AtlasTextures are already disallowed in many other places where you can use a Texture2D, so this is consistent. Pushed a build that throws an appropriate warning.

Worked with @Calinou on his above comment - the issues were all rooted in the GDScript/GDShader code, not the DrawableTexture build.

The inspector was constantly being rebuilt, and thus inaccessible, because `material_override.albedo_texture = drawable_texture` was being called in the process step of the tool GDScript, unnecessarily rebuilding the material every process step. The fade to black was due to GPU reading garbage data into an uninitialized color vector in the GDShader. Initializing the vectors to a default in the GDShader code resolved the issue.

